{
  "name": "Webhook Dedupe · 9 Lab",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Webhook Dedupe · Lab\nSix ways to claim an event, one webhook each: `POST dedupe/lab/<method>` with `{ \"event_key\": \"...\" }`. The answer is `{ claimed: true }` when this call was let through.\n\nThis workflow is for measuring, not for production. The tests send one key 40 times at once and count how many calls were let through. Use the two receiver workflows for real traffic.\n\n- `dt-check-then-insert`: Data Table: If Row Does Not Exist, then Insert\n- `dt-upsert`: Data Table: Upsert, let through when the row is new\n- `dt-insert-then-first`: Data Table: Insert, then read the first row for the key\n- `remove-duplicates`: Remove Duplicates: Remove Items Processed in Previous Executions\n- `pg-on-conflict`: Postgres: INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING RETURNING\n- `pg-unique-error`: Postgres: plain INSERT, unique violation on the error output",
        "width": 760,
        "height": 340,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "f15054b0-d3b1-4474-8c53-c4434121d263",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -420
      ]
    },
